==Korean==

===Etymology 1===
{{anchor|dog}}
{{ko-etym-native|gy|家稀}}
From {{inh|ko|oko|犬伊|tr=*KAhi}}.

{{ko-etym-native|wc|가히〮|kàhí|hangul=y|dot=,}} and subsequently recorded as {{okm-l|개〯|kǎy}} in the 16th century, after the ''h'' had dropped.<ref>{{cite-book|last=Lee|first=Ki-Moon|last2=Ramsey|first2=S. Robert|title=A History of the Korean Language|publisher=Cambridge University Press|year=2011|isbn=978-0-521-66189-8|page=163–164}}</ref>

The prefix derives from the noun. Compare {{ncog|en|bitch}}.

[[Image:YellowLabradorLooking_new.jpg|thumb|'''개'''<br>A ''dog'']]

====Pronunciation====
{{ko-IPA|l=y|a=y}}
* {{ko-tone|L_reg}}

====Noun====
{{ko-noun|count=마리}}

# [[dog]]
# {{lb|ko|figuratively|derogatory}} [[someone]] who behaves [[bad]]ly
#: {{ux|ko|[[걔]][[-는]] [[술]] [[취하다|취하]][[-면]] '''개'''[[-가]] [[되다|돼]].|t=He becomes a '''total wreck''' when he's drunk [e.g. throwing up, rambling annoyingly, etc.]|q=colloquial}}
# {{lb|ko|figuratively}} [[someone]] who does the [[bidding]] of [[another]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Some younger speakers prefer {{m|ko|강아지|t=[[puppy]]}} to refer to dogs of any age, to avoid the vulgar connotations of the prefix.

